#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:5
#: fcc6dce34ac345a2a465de9f60716e7f
msgid "Intel RealSense T265"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:12
#: b3511c0473be4274861c351d9312995a
msgid "This article explains how to setup an `Intel Realsense T265 <https://store.intelrealsense.com/buy-intel-realsense-tracking-camera-t265.html?_ga=2.225595998.511560227.1566178471-459370638.1562639781>`__ for use with ArduPilot as a substitute for a GPS allowing position control modes like Loiter, PosHold, RTL, Auto to work. This method uses a python script running on an RPI companion computer to send position information to ArduPilot without the use of `ROS <https://www.ros.org/>`__.  The `setup using ROS is here <https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.html>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:15
#: 1b99b4ae236a467a851d9cfde1add328
msgid "What to Buy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:17
#: e6545280b89445758ebc705e6bca26b7
msgid "`Intel RealSense Tracking Camera T265 <https://www.intelrealsense.com/tracking-camera-t265/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:18
#: d1e2efb7fb0b4b1790d48d91b012906c
msgid "`Raspberry Pi 4 <https://www.raspberrypi.org/products/raspberry-pi-4-model-b/>`__ (2GB or 4GB recommended, 8GB has issues) or `Raspberry Pi 3 <https://www.raspberrypi.org/products/raspberry-pi-3-model-b/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:19
#: 8b4b2df954094c6689670c29113d1771
msgid "16GB (or larger) SD card"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:20
#: baae1955963543199eef3aa22fe61924
msgid "`PiConnectLite <https://www.rpanion.com/product/pi-connect-lite-v2/>`__ to connect the RPI to the autopilot (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:24
#: fce8c94e5e8749c7bc6ce4045a278df6
msgid "The RPI4 supports USB3 which allows both **pose** + **image** data to be captured from the camera.  The slower RPI3 only has USB2 meaning only **pose** data can be captured although this is sufficient for most users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:27
#: a0526d404d61469eaa96e6fb8d564a21
msgid "Hardware Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:33
#: b13a557c501845ff8cd91af21416ac12
msgid "Download the latest APSync Ubuntu image (`found here <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Companion/apsync/apsync-rpi-ubuntu-t265-latest.img.xz>`__) to your PC and then flash it to the 16GB (or larger) SD card using a tool such as `Etcher <https://www.balena.io/etcher/>`__ or `Win32DiskImager <https://sourceforge.net/projects/win32diskimager/>`__ and then insert it into the RPI's SD Card slot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:34
#: 3915d1e063c941e494558fa8ec1d1423
msgid "Mount the Intel RealSense T265 on the vehicle facing forward (see below for information other orientations) using thick double sided tape or `David Sastre's T265 mount <https://www.dropbox.com/s/e3ias30czsn2q4t/Intel_RealSense_Tracking_Camera_T265_holder.STL?dl=0>`__ to better isolate the camera from vibrations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:35
#: 37739bfb93384301a6aaa39c83ce52d7
msgid "Connect the Intel RealSense T265's USB cable to one of the RPI4's blue USB3 ports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:36
#: bf42c356a0ac4b769803b46e68088ed1
msgid "Connect the PiConnectLite's power cable to the battery (7V to 30V)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:37
#: 6b579a434d4741dc8e1d1ea71e634e4b
msgid "Connect the PiConnectLite's serial cable to one of the autopilot's telemetry ports (i.e. Telem1, Telem2). The only signals used in this cable are TX, RX and GND. The other signals are NC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:43
#: 437e8c5cfbfe40d4af8ca1e77880947f
msgid "`David Sastre's T265 mount <https://www.dropbox.com/s/e3ias30czsn2q4t/Intel_RealSense_Tracking_Camera_T265_holder.STL?dl=0>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:46
#: e078fb718fcc4bb8b89af998b1df61f1
msgid "Configure ArduPilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:48
#: 1d4a7ed84e0e42c9912fed06ead4ee96
msgid "Connect to the autopilot with a ground station (i.e. Mission Planner) and check that the following parameters are set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:50
#: b25f653a80644fbf8ba2307732845eb0
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL <SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 2 (MAVLink2).  Note this assumes the RPI4 is connected to AutoPilot \"Telem2\" port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:51
#: d4054de3f9414b74af8b60de686ee754
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL2_BAUD <SERIAL2_BAUD>` = 921 (921600 baud)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:52
#: 2930999f08ed49e98c79d55b75a195f9
msgid "Optionally set :ref:`SERIAL2_OPTIONS <SERIAL2_OPTIONS>` = 1024 (Don't forward mavlink to/from) to block the RPI4/T265 mavlink messages from reaaching the ground station"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:53
#: f19858596e6b46ef8bfa243c5b51ac97
msgid ":ref:`VISO_TYPE <VISO_TYPE>` = 2 (IntelT265)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:55
#: 8368935f815343b8bb4f4c8c40976d57
msgid "Next setup the EKF3 to use the ExternalNav for position and velocity:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:57
#: 8f20a39203db4e24b063c5cfc08f1b61
msgid ":ref:`EK3_SRC1_POSXY <EK3_SRC1_POSXY>` = 6 (ExternalNav)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:58
#: 17bda4c3e9a54b9699a0b314224b596f
msgid ":ref:`EK3_SRC1_VELXY <EK3_SRC1_VELXY>` = 6 (ExternalNav)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:59
#: 59bf481bc8f64ddc93fe5eb0ad88aa1e
msgid ":ref:`EK3_SRC1_POSZ <EK3_SRC1_POSZ>` = 1 (Baro which is safer because of the camera's weakness to high vibrations)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:60
#: a9888aefe5fa46b9affe823ebb997916
msgid ":ref:`EK3_SRC1_VELZ <EK3_SRC1_VELZ>` = 6 (ExternalNav)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:61
#: 0b16ed7af4f84d6cb36b3e97c47e41e2
msgid "Optionally set :ref:`GPS1_TYPE <GPS1_TYPE>`  = 0 to disable the GPS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:63
#: fad8dcd942e9401f9a58dcad6f2b8c7d
msgid "If you wish to use the camera's heading:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:65
#: 2377077b698444dab98a0780de1de6cc
msgid ":ref:`COMPASS_USE <COMPASS_USE>` = 0, :ref:`COMPASS_USE2 <COMPASS_USE2>` = 0, :ref:`COMPASS_USE3<COMPASS_USE3>` = 0 to disable all compasses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:66
#: f7aa92080e4948f7a773b00e4dfdb290
msgid ":ref:`EK3_SRC1_YAW <EK3_SRC1_YAW>` = 6 (ExternalNav)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:68
#: aa2dc13bb27e401fab81c66514237fa9
msgid "If you wish to use the autopilot's compass for heading:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:70
#: d91a3177c44d4c2f9e6f12c26803fc25
msgid ":ref:`COMPASS_USE <COMPASS_USE>` = 1 (the default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:71
#: 10b934ab2a484409999d60216488b462
msgid ":ref:`EK3_SRC1_YAW <EK3_SRC1_YAW>` = 1 (Compass)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:72
#: 03668f7e0a20408bb81abe6e46f16101
msgid ":ref:`RC7_OPTION <RC7_OPTION>` = 80 (Viso Align) to allow the pilot to re-align the camera's yaw with the AHRS/EKF yaw before flight with auxiliary switch 7.  Re-aligning yaw before takeoff is a good idea or loss of position control (aka \"toilet bowling\") may occur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:74
#: 3a78557f7d00487bae67e89e9872a281
msgid "After the parameters are modified, reboot the autopilot.  Connect with the ground station and (if using Mission Planner) right-mouse-button-click on the map, select \"Set Home Here\", \"Set EKF Origin Here\" to tell ArduPilot where the vehicle is and it should instantly appear on the map."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:76
#: d496b1aaf160496cacf544949e6325d2
msgid "Just before flying, pick up the vehicle to a height of 1m and then put it down again.  This allows the camera to calibrate its vertical scaling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:78
#: 612ee200632a464dab67ba2b1f311fa4
msgid "If you wish to switch between GPS and T265 see the :ref:`GPS/Non-GPS Transitions <common-non-gps-to-gps>` wiki page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:81
#: c4a8b503a0414947a65210e7eda87913
msgid "System Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:86
#: f8067c6482b8474ba725b64582284cd8
msgid "In a nutshell, the 6-DOF pose data (**position** and **orientation**) and **confidence level** obtained from the Realsense T265 will be processed by our python script and send to ArduPilot through MAVLink. Overall, the script will do the following tasks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:88
#: 6f2bcc4e2efc464083fa4825f43c6d92
msgid "Obtain 6-DOF pose data and tracking confidence level data using relevant APIs from ``pyrealsense2``, which is the Python wrapper for ``librealsense``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:89
#: da4e5ecebb1e4e0991127211540cd7f9
msgid "Perform necessary matrix transformation to align the frames of the Realsense T265 and NED frame as well as other processing steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:90
#: 664956f24b2043fc91f3f82ec8ab28c3
msgid "Pack pose data into MAVLink message `VISION_POSITION_ESTIMATE <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#VISION_POSITION_ESTIMATE>`__ and confidence level data into a dummy message, then send them to ArduPilot at a predetermined frequency so as to not `flood` the Autopilot with incoming data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:91
#: 468408498cf148658c352a2d96d685ab
msgid "Automatically set EKF home for simple setup and flying."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:95
#: 6aafd97d5e2e4c80b90c9b3e414544da
msgid "The choice of Python is optional, and you can use any `other wrappers supported by librealsense <https://github.com/IntelRealSense/librealsense/tree/master/wrappers#wrappers-for-intel-realsense-technology>`__. ROS users can find the equivalent article :ref:`here <ros-vio-tracking-camera>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:100
#: e008c7a3783546f393ab3618df990f7b
msgid "For the sake of brevity, explanation of the system will be kept short. More in-depth discussion can be found in the following blog posts: `part 4 <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/t/integration-of-ardupilot-and-vio-tracking-camera-part-4-non-ros-bridge-to-mavlink-in-python/44001>`__, `part 5 <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/t/integration-of-ardupilot-and-vio-tracking-camera-part-5-camera-position-offsets-compensation-scale-calibration-and-compass-north-alignment-beta/44984>`__."
msgstr ""

